# ---- private corpora ----
# An allow-list, not a list of known dataset names. A deny-list was wrong here already:
# `data/raw/` and `data/exports/` were ignored while `data/mpower/` was not, even though
# the asymmetry trainer's own docstring tells you to put real mPower records in it. Anything
# that appears under data/ is real corpus material until a human decides otherwise, so the
# directory is ignored wholesale and the one reviewed file is re-admitted by name.
data/*
!data/README.md
backend/data/

# ---- model weights and per-patient adapters ----
# Also an allow-list. The previous rule enumerated weight extensions, which left `.wav`,
# `.gguf`, `tokenizer.json` and any README stageable inside a per-patient adapter directory
# -- and a patient WAV under artifacts/ is precisely the INV-1 failure this repo exists to
# prevent. Everything here is a generated runtime artifact except the five reviewed metric
# fixtures, which are named back in. Subdirectories stay ignored entirely: git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a per-patient adapter dir cannot be re-admitted
# by accident.
backend/app/ml/train/artifacts/**
!backend/app/ml/train/artifacts/*.metrics.json

# ---- Awaaz local exports ----
# These contain consented patient audio and must never leave the device. The extension is
# matched loosely on purpose: `.tar.gz`, `.tgz`, `.zip` and `.tar.enc` all escaped a rule
# that only knew about `.tar`.
awaaz-training*
*awaaz*training*

# --- PRIVACY: real patient source material (never committed) ---
#
# The reference-patient photographs live in the working tree, NOT outside the repo as was
# assumed. They are photographs of a real person's medical records. These rules are
# defensive and deliberately broad: the cost of a false positive is a developer renaming an
# asset, the cost of a false negative is publishing someone's medical records to GitHub.
#
# Enforced by tests/test_privacy.py, which fails the build if any of them becomes tracked.
# Source medical photographs. NO TRAILING SLASH — it used to be `*stroke report*/`, which
# matches directories only, so `real stroke report.zip` (an archive of all 22 photographs)
# was ignored solely by the `*.zip` build-artifact rule above. Narrow or remove that rule
# and somebody's hospital records become stageable. Two independent rules now cover it.
*stroke report*
*stroke report*.zip
*.jpeg
*.jpg

# Local-only list of real identifiers used by tests/test_privacy.py. Never committed.
.privacy-denylist

# Local database backups taken before each migration. They contain seeded demo data and
# are binary snapshots of whatever the dev DB held at the time — never publish them.
.backups/

# Throwaway probes
frontend/scratch/

# Playwright MCP session artefacts + root-level screenshots
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# Throwaway browser-sweep scripts written next to the app during debugging.
frontend/*.mjs
